<title>USA: IPO PRICING - FaxSav at $8.</title>
<headline>IPO PRICING - FaxSav at $8.</headline>
<dateline>EDISON, N.J. 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>FaxSav Inc said its shares had priced at $8 each for the company's initial public offering of 1.5 million shares.</p>
<p>All shares were sold by FaxSav. The offering is being managed by Lehman Brothers Inc and Alex. Brown &amp; Sons Inc.</p>
<p>The company makes business-to-business facsimile transmission services, including fax-to-fax, desktop-to-fax, enhanced fax and broadcast services. Its services are designed to cut the cost and time of sending an international fax by using an Internet-based network, allowing users to bypass long-distance carriers' networks when sending faxes.</p>
<p>Net proceeds from the offering will be used expand the company's network, repay existing short-term debt, and for general corporate purposes, the company said in a release.</p>
</text>
